---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AREDN_URL, GREENSIGHT_URL, LINKEDIN_URL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Experience"
	description="Work, startups, and selected projects — Amazon, GreenSight, and beyond."
>
	<main>
		<header class="page-header">
			<h1>Experience</h1>
			<p class="muted">
				Selected roles and projects. For the full ladder and dates, see{' '}
				<a href={LINKEDIN_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>Professional</h2>

			<h3>Amazon</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>Software Development Engineer II</strong> (Mar 2026 – Present) ·{' '}
				<strong>SDE I</strong> (Sep 2024 – Mar 2026) · San Luis Obispo
			</p>
			<p>
				I build payment reporting and invoicing systems for vendors on Amazon’s digital marketplaces
				(Prime Video, Amazon Music, KDP, Merch, and more) — high-availability microservice work with
				measurable operational impact.
			</p>
			<p>
				Earlier on the Junior Developer track (<strong>Jr. Software Developer I–III</strong>, Dec
				2021 – Jun 2024), I contributed full-stack with Java, Angular, and React, including an AWS
				Lambda path for automated vendor invoice notifications.
			</p>

			<h3>
				<a href={GREENSIGHT_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">GreenSight Technologies</a>
			</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>Co-founder &amp; Engineering Lead</strong> (Jan 2024 – Sep 2024), including the Cal Poly
				Summer Accelerator.
			</p>
			<p>
				Architected an AI-driven multi-tenant platform for electronics recyclers and resellers —
				identification, pricing, and ops insights. Delivered a production-ready beta to three
				businesses (React, React Native, Cloudflare, applied ML).
			</p>

			<h3>Cal Poly ITS</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>Service Desk Student Lead</strong> (Jul 2021 – Dec 2021), after starting as a Student
				Assistant (Mar 2021 – Jun 2021). Led student staff, handled in-person troubleshooting, and represented
				the desk in campus outage response (Slack, Confluence, JIRA).
			</p>

			<h3>Wilson Creek Communications</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>Network Engineering Intern</strong> (Jul 2019 – Aug 2020). Maintained rural WISP infrastructure
				across many sites, helped migrate backends to VMware ESXi, and wrote Python tooling for AP coverage
				planning.
			</p>

			<hr />

			<h2>FRC Team 973 — The Greybots</h2>
			<p>
				Programmer and later mentor with{' '}
				<a href="https://greybots.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">Team 973</a>
				{' '}(2016–2020 as a student; mentored in college). Competition software in C++/Java, plus
				tools like a real-time robot dashboard and a Sheets-backed attendance app. Team highlights
				include world championship hardware and a 4th-place Worlds finish while mentoring — the
				through-line is shipping reliable code under pressure and teaching others to do the same.
			</p>

			<hr />

			<h2>Homelab &amp; side projects</h2>
			<p>
				Ongoing lab for networking, home automation, containers, and TrueNAS storage — the same
				curiosity shows up in radio (W6BHZ /{' '}
				<a href={AREDN_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">AREDN</a>
				) and embedded experiments like an automated coop door (Arduino + Pi). Writing about these builds
				lives on the{' '}
				<a href="/blog">blog</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
	.page-header {
		margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
	}

	.page-header p {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 36rem;
	}
</style>
